## Tests

```bash
just test claims-gateway
```

| File | What it checks |
|---|---|
| `service/exchange_test.go` | Current memberships signed. `name` before `preferred_username`. Bad ID token. `tenancy` errors fail closed on sign-in and refresh. First-login provisioning: none without an organization, empty on invite-only, failure on other errors. `HighestRole` |
| `service/register_test.go`, `service/profile_test.go` | Login, sign-up, taken email, profile edit, password checked before reset |
| `api/handler_test.go`, `register_handler_test.go`, `profile_handler_test.go` | Routes, status codes, required fields |
| `api/verify_handler_test.go` | `/verify` writes the header. The header decodes through `RequireMeshClaims`. No token is `401` |
| `signer/signer_test.go` | The token checks out as RS256. `exp` follows the lifetime. The JWKS holds the key |
| `oidcverifier/verifier_test.go` | Valid token. `name` and `organization` optional. Wrong audience, expiry, key and issuer refused. `jwks_uri` moved to the discovery host. Discovery failures |
| `keycloakadmin/client_test.go` | Each Keycloak call and its error mapping |
| `tenancyclient/client_test.go` | Signed requests. `403` becomes `ErrInviteOnly`. Failures are errors, never an empty list |
| `config/*_test.go` | Key from file. A missing file fails. Realm and secret required. Keycloak base URL |

---

## Gaps

- **A missing domain blocks sign-in.** An ID token naming an organization with no `tenancy` domain gets `404` from provision, and the person cannot sign in at all (`503`).
- **Only the first organization is used.** A person in two Keycloak organizations is provisioned in the first only.
- **A sleeping screen loses the session.** No refresh for 15 minutes means signing in again.
- **No way to revoke one token.** A stolen JWT works until `exp`. `sid` is not checked anywhere. Logout only deletes the browser's cookie.
- **Refresh never asks Keycloak.** A person disabled in Keycloak stays signed in as long as refreshes keep coming before `exp`. Only `tenancy` is asked again.
- **Boot discovery has no timeout.** `discoverJWKSURL` uses `http.DefaultClient` with the signal context, which has no deadline. A Keycloak that accepts the connection and never answers hangs the start-up instead of failing it.
- **`EmailVerified` is read and never used.** New users are created with `emailVerified: false`.
